dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:37:- **E3.** Moves like a **human**: scroll DEEP (many screens, full results), view options at higher frequency but **human cadence** (dwell between actions). This also avoids Dribbble's bot-check that rapid machine-nav triggers.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:39:- **E5.** Quality over quota - reject logos, light-mode, consumer/mobile, coding-challenge, glass/gradient.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:47:- **G1. Operator reference-review gate (standing, until trust established):** after the Dribbble agent gathers + before convergence/council runs, present the candidate pool to the operator for relevance review. Convergence does not run on an un-reviewed pool.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:49:- **G3. Paid-call gate:** at each paid Anthropic boundary, surface the plan + cost and explain the advantage before firing; no unilateral paid calls.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:50:- **G4.** Operator reviews surviving references before the elevation loop runs.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:51:- **G5.** Operator approves applying elevated output to the live `~/.claude/powerline-config/` config.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:55:- **H2.** Free no-LLM smoke de-risks the loop plumbing before paid spawns.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:64:1. Skills-first brief (4 skill-agents -> synthesis) [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:65:2. Dribbble agent gathers pool, live + watchable [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:66:3. **Operator reviews pool** [gate G1/G2]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:67:4. Unanimous convergence on reviewed pool [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:68:5. **Operator reviews survivors** [gate G4]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:69:6. Elevation loop per element, refs as context [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:71:8. **Operator approves apply to live** [gate G5]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:76:- **K3.** Whether the skills-first brief (Phase 1, 4 paid skill-agents) is wanted every run, or cached/reused across runs for the same project.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:82:- **L1. Order reversed (locked):** gather -> **operator approves the gathered pool/collection** (relevance/validity) -> convergence (skill-fit, unanimous) -> final refs -> operator review -> elevate. HIL is intentionally heavy now and steps down gradually as trust builds.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:83:- **L2. Collection-based gather (recommended + adopted):** the Dribbble agent creates ONE project-named **collection** and saves candidates to it via the **ribbon (save-to-collection)** button (hover or in-modal) - NOT the global heart-like, to keep the account tidy. Over-gather broadly; the collection is the durable, operator-viewable candidate pool.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:84:- **L3. Convergence input = the collection:** screenshot the collection grid as thumbnails + open key shots for genuine evaluation; the **4 skill-agents converge (unanimous)** on it. (Chosen over the agent self-narrowing - honors skills-converge.)
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:88:  - **Related:** follow the page's `Related:` terms to branch into adjacent searches (human-like discovery) past the primary query.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:89:- **L5. Counts/bounds (proposed, confirm):** searches min 4 / max ~8 (incl. Related branches); collection over-gather ~12-18 candidates; final references presented min 3 (>=1 per element where possible) / target 5-6 / max 8.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/REQUIREMENTS.md:91:- **L7. PREREQUISITE - Dribbble login:** collections + saving require the operator's Chrome to be **logged into Dribbble**. Favoriting/collection actions are benign, reversible content-curation on the operator's own account, authorized by the operator. (The earlier human-check was cleared; login state must be confirmed before the collection flow.)
