dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:548:**Next = R-FS-1 → B5 (memory backend per deployment surface)** — `built-but-vacuous` (grounding sweep Arc B5; `[[built-but-vacuous-reground-ledger-asis]]`). `MemoryToolRegistry.resolve_backend(deployment_surface)` is BUILT + production-wired (called at `llm_dispatch.py` on the Anthropic Memory-tool path) but DEGENERATE: its body is `return self._backend` — it drops its discriminating argument; the registry stores ONE bootstrap-frozen backend. R-830 ✅ already made FILESYSTEM + SQLite + S3 + managed-DB backends live in the factory's construct-step, so the backends B5 routes to ALL EXIST; B5 only adds the surface→backend dispatch the registry currently lacks (a surface→backend map resolved once at bootstrap stage 5). **Thin impl, no fork** (impl-discretion). Re-ground at arc-open (grounding sweep Arc B5, presence-not-correctness; body-read `memory_tool_registry.py` + the stage-5 factory at HEAD; the single `deployment_surface` value threaded today makes the dropped arg doubly inert). **CA ✅ COMPLETE (#625)** — `RunResult.cost_attribution` populated (runtime spec v1.53 §9; `CostRecordAccumulator` holder + 4 per-dispatch wrappers + `_build_run_result` PER_PROVIDER_AND_MODEL rollup; Pydantic-freeze-copy bug caught by advisor + guarded). Frozen order: B1✅ B3✅ E✅ B2✅ R✅ B4✅ **CA✅** → **B5 (next)** → B6 → B7 → M. **Forward items registered:** `B-COST-DISCRIMINATOR-TAXONOMY` (CA #625 — dispatch-type `provider_discriminator` tags ∉ `CrossFamilyTag` block the per-family rollup); `B-NONLINEAR-OVERRIDE-PROVENANCE` (B4 #621 — per-step override-ledger entry linear-only).
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:552:**Do not re-open as next action.** Closed/parked: `R-411/412/420/421/430`, `R-500`, `R-810/820/830`, `R-008`/OD-4, `R-CXA-1/2/4`, `R-100-*`, `R-300-*` (both routing-activation #213 and second-provider #281/#283 RESOLVED), `R-901` (research frontier closed). `R-CL-Q1→C1` (quality track) BLOCKED behind R-FS-1 (full-spec runs once, on the complete harness).
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:562:**Frozen order** (B1→B3→E→B2→R→B4→CA→B5→B6→B7→M). DONE: **B1✅ B3✅ E✅ B2✅ R✅ B4✅ CA✅** (R incl. L3 LLM_AS_ROUTER #604 + L2 EMBEDDING #606; B4 incl. Slice 1✅#616 / 2✅#618 / 3✅#619 / 4✅#621; CA✅#625 runtime spec v1.53 §9). NEXT: **B5 (memory backend per deployment surface)** → then B6 → B7 → M. Plus **9 standalone design-fork-first `B-*` arcs** (incl. `B-COST-DISCRIMINATOR-TAXONOMY` #625, `B-NONLINEAR-OVERRIDE-PROVENANCE` #621) and the visibility-only **routing-activation gate** (UNOWNED until a second production provider is configured) — both detailed in the arc-and-unit map.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:578:| PR #625 | 2026-06-17 | **feat(runtime): R-FS-1 arc CA — populate `RunResult.cost_attribution` (per-run cost rollup; runtime spec v1.52→v1.53 §9 C-RT-09).** The run-result cost field (hard-coded `()` since landing behind the now-CLOSED U-OD-21 HALTED tension) is now populated: a run-scoped `CostRecordAccumulator` holder on `HarnessContext` is threaded into the LLM/tool/validator/webhook per-dispatch cost wrappers (each appends its returned `SpanCostRecord`); `_build_run_result` rolls up along `RollupAxis.PER_PROVIDER_AND_MODEL` (single axis ⟹ `sum(total_cost)` = true run cost). **Axis empirically forced** (advisor + HEAD body-grounding overturned the grounding-sweep's `PER_PROVIDER_DISCRIMINATOR` lead): production cost helpers tag `provider_discriminator` with dispatch-type tags (`"llm"`/`"tool"`/`"validator"`/`"webhook"`), none `CrossFamilyTag` members, so that axis raises `CrossFamilyRollupError` → latent mismatch registered as forward arc `B-COST-DISCRIMINATOR-TAXONOMY` (the dispatch-type breakdown is the most operator-meaningful rollup + exactly the one it blocks). **Critical bug caught pre-merge** (advisor, decorrelated): the first impl used a typed `list[...]` field, which Pydantic v2 COPIES at `freeze()` (`M(xs=lst).xs is not lst`) → the frozen ctx held a different list than the dispatchers captured → `cost_attribution` always `()` in production, invisible to every test not traversing `freeze()` (the §13.1 green-but-unreachable-through-bootstrap failure mode). Fixed with the by-reference `CostRecordAccumulator` holder (arbitrary type, like `drained_flag`/`tracer_provider`) + `test_bootstrap_cost_accumulator_survives_freeze_by_reference` (asserts the bare tool dispatcher's sink IS `ctx.cost_record_accumulator.records`). Webhook cost is pre-existing-inert (v1.26 empty-marker factory binds no cost substrates; sink forward-ready, dormant until FM-2). **Bundled-absorption** (runtime spec v1.53 + fork + clearance + spine; additive/clarifying — NO operator gate, sacrifices no committed invariant; X-AL-3 green). All 4 wrappers proven append by-execution + rollup math + single-axis sum-invariant + `_build_run_result` populate/empty + the freeze-by-ref seam regression test. **advisor** caught the freeze-copy bug + confirmed the holder fix; **Codex** clean ("threaded consistently, no introduced correctness issues"). harness-runtime 1803 passed / 10 skipped; CXA-P1 34; overlay 31/31; pyright 0/0/0 touched; ruff clean; all CI blocking checks pass. → NEXT = **B5 (memory backend per deployment surface)**. |
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:579:| PR #623 | 2026-06-17 | **fix(dashboard): reflect B4 completion in the arc-and-unit-map (build-progress source) + add it to the deploy trigger.** The published roadmap showed CONFLICTING B4 signals — `roadmap_status.md`-derived sections said "B4✅ → CA next" but the build-progress masthead / arc-strip / per-arc cards (parsed from `.harness/r-fs-1-arc-and-unit-map.md`) still said "5/11, NEXT = B4". Root cause: the arc-and-unit-map (the dashboard's single arc→unit source) was never refreshed through ANY B4 slice (1-4), AND it was not in the `dashboard-deploy.yml` path filter, so updates to it never auto-deployed (the deploy regenerates from sources). Fix: arc-map B4 → ✅ done (position 6/11) with as-built units (the 4 slices keyed by PR #616/#618/#619/#621, which extended C-CP-06 / C-RT-15 / C-IS-05 rather than minting new plan-units); CA → ▶ NEXT (7/11); build-order summary, serial-cluster line, unblocked line, §7 at-a-glance all updated; `generate.py` renders a 0-new-unit as-built arc as "N build legs (slices)" not a misleading "0 atomic units"; `dashboard-deploy.yml` adds `.harness/r-fs-1-arc-and-unit-map.md` to the path filter (the structural gap). Verified by **in-browser render** (the #608/#612 lesson): masthead "6 / 11 arcs done", arc strip B1✓…R✓ B4✓ → CA•next, arc map B4 ✓ DONE / CA ▶ NEXT, no console errors. 14 dashboard tests + ruff green; all CI blocking checks pass. Mode-agnostic; X-AL-3 trivially clean. → NEXT = **CA (cost aggregate)** (unchanged). |
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:580:| PR #621 | 2026-06-17 | **feat(cp): R-FS-1 B4 Slice 4 — per-step ROLE override + linear-path role indexing (CP v1.38 / runtime v1.52 §14.5.3 relaxation) — closes the B4 tail.** A per-step `StepOverride.agent_role` assigns a specialist role to a specific step — overriding the B1 fan-out-derived role on a branch, or supplying a role on the `SINGLE_THREADED_LINEAR` path (which carries none today). **Mechanism = Option B (composition-time fold):** the CP driver folds the override onto the single `StepExecutionContext.agent_role` source at all 6 topology composition sites (precedence per-step > fan-out-derived > default); the **runtime dispatch read is byte-unchanged** — the C-RT-16 wrapper picks up the role for MODEL (`_effective_chain`) + the C-RT-15 inner for PROMPT from one source (zero `harness-runtime` impl edit; the `default_gate_level → parent_gate_level` v1.20 precedent). **OPERATOR-RATIFIED** (AskUserQuestion "Ratify full" 2026-06-17) — a committed-invariant relaxation (runtime v1.52 §14.5.3 invariant-2 "single role source" + invariant-3 "linear path untouched"; invariant-1 non-breaking-default preserved — absent override → byte-identical) is the operator's call. advisor reversed a probe-resolves attempt to dissolve the gate (the decisive asymmetry: `default_gate_level` had no invariant forbidding it, role has the explicit §14.5.3 invariant 2). **Bundled-absorption** (CP spec v1.37→v1.38 additive `StepOverride.agent_role` + `StepEffectiveBinding` propagation + §6.6 provenance extension; runtime v1.51→v1.52 §14.5.3 relaxation; fork + 2 clearance markers + spine; X-AL-3 green). Provenance at the WIRED per-step override state-ledger entry (`binding.model_dump`), NOT the §5.2 hash (no IS-spec change). **Codex** caught a PRE-EXISTING non-linear override-ledger provenance gap (linear-only emission across model/prompt/role) → scoped honestly in §6.6 + registered as the `B-NONLINEAR-OVERRIDE-PROVENANCE` forward arc (routing correct on every topology; only the override-audit-entry is linear-only) — NOT scope-crept; + the [P3] empty-role truthiness (kept deliberately, dispatch-consistent); re-review clean. Verified: CP unit + linear-path by-execution + fan-out override-replaces-derived + **full-stack consumer-e2e** (per-step role → driver-fold → real wrapper+inner → provider gets BOTH override-role model= AND system=). pyright 0/0/0; ruff clean; harness-cp 1045 passed / 1 xfailed; harness-runtime 1594 non-integration + 210 integration; overlay 31/31. → NEXT = **CA (cost aggregate)**. |
