dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:697:- For credential-gated units, build to the exact credential boundary, prove all non-credential forward actions are closed, then log the gate with `just codex-credential-gate --unit ... --gate ... --forward-closed ... --resume ...` if no HIL/operator-approval surface is available. Update a human-facing tracking surface so the pending gate is visible on the next human engagement, then proceed to the next implementable unit.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:852:- **E3.** Moves like a **human**: scroll DEEP (many screens, full results), view options at higher frequency but **human cadence** (dwell between actions). This also avoids Dribbble's bot-check that rapid machine-nav triggers.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:854:- **E5.** Quality over quota - reject logos, light-mode, consumer/mobile, coding-challenge, glass/gradient.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:862:- **G1. Operator reference-review gate (standing, until trust established):** after the Dribbble agent gathers + before convergence/council runs, present the candidate pool to the operator for relevance review. Convergence does not run on an un-reviewed pool.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:864:- **G3. Paid-call gate:** at each paid Anthropic boundary, surface the plan + cost and explain the advantage before firing; no unilateral paid calls.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:865:- **G4.** Operator reviews surviving references before the elevation loop runs.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:866:- **G5.** Operator approves applying elevated output to the live `~/.claude/powerline-config/` config.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:870:- **H2.** Free no-LLM smoke de-risks the loop plumbing before paid spawns.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:879:1. Skills-first brief (4 skill-agents -> synthesis) [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:880:2. Dribbble agent gathers pool, live + watchable [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:881:3. **Operator reviews pool** [gate G1/G2]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:882:4. Unanimous convergence on reviewed pool [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:883:5. **Operator reviews survivors** [gate G4]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:884:6. Elevation loop per element, refs as context [paid; gate G3]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:886:8. **Operator approves apply to live** [gate G5]
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:891:- **K3.** Whether the skills-first brief (Phase 1, 4 paid skill-agents) is wanted every run, or cached/reused across runs for the same project.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:897:- **L1. Order reversed (locked):** gather -> **operator approves the gathered pool/collection** (relevance/validity) -> convergence (skill-fit, unanimous) -> final refs -> operator review -> elevate. HIL is intentionally heavy now and steps down gradually as trust builds.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:898:- **L2. Collection-based gather (recommended + adopted):** the Dribbble agent creates ONE project-named **collection** and saves candidates to it via the **ribbon (save-to-collection)** button (hover or in-modal) - NOT the global heart-like, to keep the account tidy. Over-gather broadly; the collection is the durable, operator-viewable candidate pool.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:899:- **L3. Convergence input = the collection:** screenshot the collection grid as thumbnails + open key shots for genuine evaluation; the **4 skill-agents converge (unanimous)** on it. (Chosen over the agent self-narrowing - honors skills-converge.)
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:903:  - **Related:** follow the page's `Related:` terms to branch into adjacent searches (human-like discovery) past the primary query.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:904:- **L5. Counts/bounds (proposed, confirm):** searches min 4 / max ~8 (incl. Related branches); collection over-gather ~12-18 candidates; final references presented min 3 (>=1 per element where possible) / target 5-6 / max 8.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:906:- **L7. PREREQUISITE - Dribbble login:** collections + saving require the operator's Chrome to be **logged into Dribbble**. Favoriting/collection actions are benign, reversible content-curation on the operator's own account, authorized by the operator. (The earlier human-check was cleared; login state must be confirmed before the collection flow.)
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:920:You select design references from Dribbble for a specific project, grounding every pick in BOTH the project build context (below) and the deep design knowledge of four installed skills. You drive a **visible** Chrome window so the human can watch the search and selection happen live. You are a curator, not a yes-machine: most shots should be rejected.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:940:REJECT - do not select: standalone logos / brand-identity mockups; light-mode UIs; consumer/mobile app screens; coding-challenge or marketing pages; glassmorphism, glow, lens-flare, gradient-drenched "AI/SaaS" looks; large rounded cards; multi-color status confetti. These are off-brand for a precise warm-dark instrument tool.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:952:A reference is SELECTED only if it would survive all four lenses (the human's standing bar is unanimous-quality). State, per pick, what each relevant lens endorses.
