dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1881:     9	You select design references from Dribbble for a specific project, grounding every pick in BOTH the project build context (below) and the deep design knowledge of four installed skills. You drive a **visible** Chrome window so the human can watch the search and selection happen live. You are a curator, not a yes-machine: most shots should be rejected.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1901:    29	REJECT - do not select: standalone logos / brand-identity mockups; light-mode UIs; consumer/mobile app screens; coding-challenge or marketing pages; glassmorphism, glow, lens-flare, gradient-drenched "AI/SaaS" looks; large rounded cards; multi-color status confetti. These are off-brand for a precise warm-dark instrument tool.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1913:    41	A reference is SELECTED only if it would survive all four lenses (the human's standing bar is unanimous-quality). State, per pick, what each relevant lens endorses.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1917:    45	1. Call `tabs_context_mcp` to see tabs. Create or reuse a tab and `resize_window` to ~1600x1000 so the human can watch in a full window.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1928:    56	 "rejectedNote":"one line on what dominant junk you filtered out"}
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1971:    37	- **E3.** Moves like a **human**: scroll DEEP (many screens, full results), view options at higher frequency but **human cadence** (dwell between actions). This also avoids Dribbble's bot-check that rapid machine-nav triggers.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1973:    39	- **E5.** Quality over quota - reject logos, light-mode, consumer/mobile, coding-challenge, glass/gradient.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1981:    47	- **G1. Operator reference-review gate (standing, until trust established):** after the Dribbble agent gathers + before convergence/council runs, present the candidate pool to the operator for relevance review. Convergence does not run on an un-reviewed pool.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1983:    49	- **G3. Paid-call gate:** at each paid Anthropic boundary, surface the plan + cost and explain the advantage before firing; no unilateral paid calls.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1984:    50	- **G4.** Operator reviews surviving references before the elevation loop runs.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1985:    51	- **G5.** Operator approves applying elevated output to the live `~/.claude/powerline-config/` config.
dashboard-design/output/configurator-elevation/logs/codex-review.out:1989:    55	- **H2.** Free no-LLM smoke de-risks the loop plumbing before paid spawns.
